# Secrets and configuration
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json
cert.pem

# Cloudflare tunnel credentials
.cloudflared/
tunnel-*.json

# Application data -- receipts live here, never in git.
#
# ANCHORED to the repo root with a leading slash, and that is load-bearing: an
# unanchored `backups/` matches a directory of that name at ANY depth, which
# silently swallowed `apps/web/src/app/api/admin/backups/` — the whole backup
# download route and its tests — when Phase 9 added it. The feature would have
# been committed without the endpoint its button calls, and nothing would have
# failed until someone pressed it. These three only ever meant the volumes at
# the root.
/data/
/uploads/
/backups/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db

# Private working notes -- AARs, retros, threat models, real hostnames
docs/private/
*AAR*.md
*aar*.md
*RETRO*.md
NOTES.md
SCRATCH.md
TODO-private.md

